WEBVTT

00:00:03.822 --> 00:00:11.080
Trading Solutions
Open a client's trading account, take and execute an order, run the bond book and distribute research.

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:17.840
Sign in as Arvind Ramsurrun — Trader
Trader — opens accounts, takes and executes orders

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:22.440
Investments ▸ Trading Solutions ▸ Securities Accounts
Each account: client, markets, custodian, CDS and OMS numbers, limits

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:29.080
The account-opening wizard: three short steps
Client & account → custody & settlement → controls

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:35.000
Where the securities are held and where the money settles
And who may give instructions on the account

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:39.200
A trading limit — the agreement and appropriateness come later
They are ticked once the client has signed and been assessed

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:41.400
Account request created at Requested
An account number is given automatically

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:50.320
On the pipeline, move the account to KYC & appropriateness
Check the client's KYC and that she understands the products

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:53.800
Next, Agreement…
The CRM checks the signed agreement and the appropriateness test

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:57.360
Blocked: the agreement must be signed and appropriateness assessed
A stage gate — the account cannot go further without them

00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:07.400
She has signed and passed the appropriateness test — tick both
Edit the account

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:17.000
Move to Agreement again — this time it goes through
Then CDS opening: Operations requests the CDS account

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:20.480
Try to activate the account
Trading needs a CDS account number and approved KYC

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:24.000
Blocked: the CDS account number is missing
Activation also checks that the client's KYC is approved

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:34.360
The CDS has opened the account — enter its number and the OMS account
Edit the account

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:39.920
Activate again
Corinne Henry's KYC is approved, so the account goes live

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:45.840
Before taking orders: the restricted list
KYC & Compliance ▸ Restricted list — kept by Compliance, read by traders

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:50.360
Island Agro Industries Ltd is on the restricted list
Genesis advises on a deal for this issuer — no orders, no trade ideas

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:59.480
Corinne Henry phones in an order
Order Intake Log ▸ New: every instruction is time-stamped

00:01:59.480 --> 00:02:05.760
A limit order, received by phone
The time received and the voice recording reference are best-execution evidence

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:14.760
On the pipeline, move the order to Sent to OMS
The CRM hands it to the order management system

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:17.760
The OMS answered with its reference: OMS-6848180
Written on the order automatically

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:21.320
The order is filled — move it to Executed
The CRM wants the OMS reference and the executed price

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:27.280
Blocked: the executed price is missing
An order is never marked executed without the fill details

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:42.040
Enter the executed price from the OMS fill
The OMS reference is already there

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:45.600
Executed — consideration and estimated brokerage are calculated
Quantity × executed price; the client's account counts the order

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:56.800
Another client call: buy Island Agro Industries Ltd
Let's see what the CRM does

00:02:56.800 --> 00:03:01.360
Refused: this issuer is on the restricted list
The order cannot be taken — the check runs on the server, no one can skip it

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:10.480
Genesis is placing the MCB Group 2031 Notes
IPO / Bond Book: record each client's indication of interest

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:14.000
Allocated is filled in when the book closes
Demand per issue shows on the Trading dashboard

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:17.440
The book for every issue
Indicated and allocated amounts per investor

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:30.040
Publish a research note
Research & Market Statistics ▸ New

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:31.640
Send to subscribers: one click
Every active subscriber of research notes is emailed, in English or French

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:40.680
The CRM reports how many were emailed and how many skipped
Clients who unsubscribed, or have no marketing consent, are never emailed

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:47.360
Distributed is ticked and Opens starts at 0
Opens counts up as recipients read it — an estimate, some mail apps block images

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:50.640
The distribution is kept on the note's Activity timeline
Who sent it, when, and to how many subscribers

00:03:57.800 --> 00:04:01.840
An earlier note: 271 opens so far
A simple read on which research clients find useful

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:04.200
Corporate Advisory sits behind the advisory wall
Traders cannot see deals Genesis is advising on

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:08.640
The trader sees no advisory mandates
That is why the restricted list exists: Compliance tells the desk what not to trade

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:20.560
The Trading dashboard
Accounts, portfolio value, orders by market, consideration and the bond book

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:23.240
Orders by market and consideration per month
Each widget opens the records behind it

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:25.800
The IPO / bond book by issue
Including today's indication

00:04:26.809 --> 00:04:33.280
Trading Solutions
The CRM keeps the evidence and enforces the rules — the trader serves the client.
